on(a, b):\n","    result = a / b\n","    return result\n","\n","# This will raise a ZeroDivisionError\n","faulty_function(10, 0)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"idgY1ndBFPHC"},"source":["*(After running the above cell and it errors out, run the following in a new cell)*"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":34546,"status":"ok","timestamp":1749092094961,"user":{"displayName":"James Vasanth","userId":"02578488766480362375"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"7wcOnsyGFPHC","outputId":"d01b1ba3-fc0a-4122-f84d-0e5c90568457"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["> \u001b[0;32m<ipython-input-1-74a5410690b8>\u001b[0m(3)\u001b[0;36mfaulty_function\u001b[0;34m()\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0;32m      1 \u001b[0;31m\u001b[0;31m# Create a cell with an intentional error\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m      2 \u001b[0;31m\u001b[0;32mdef\u001b[0m \u001b[0mfaulty_function\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0mb\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m----> 3 \u001b[0;31m    \u001b[0mresult\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m \u001b[0ma\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m/\u001b[0m \u001b[0mb\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m      4 \u001b[0;31m    \u001b[0;32mreturn\u001b[0m \u001b[0mresult\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m      5 \u001b[0;31m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\n","ipdb> l\n","\u001b[1;32m      1 \u001b[0m\u001b[0;31m# Create a cell with an intentional error\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[1;32m      2 \u001b[0m\u001b[0;32mdef\u001b[0m \u001b[0mfaulty_function\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0mb\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0;32m----> 3 \u001b[0;31m    \u001b[0mresult\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m \u001b[0ma\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m/\u001b[0m \u001b[0mb\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m      4 \u001b[0m    \u001b[0;32mreturn\u001b[0m \u001b[0mresult\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[1;32m      5 \u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[1;32m      6 \u001b[0m\u001b[0;31m# This will raise a ZeroDivisionError\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[1;32m      7 \u001b[0m\u001b[0mfaulty_function\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0;36m10\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0;36m0\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\n","ipdb> q\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["\n","PYDEV DEBUGGER WARNING:\n","sys.settrace() should not be used when the debugger is being used.\n","This may cause the debugger to stop working correctly.\n","If this is needed, please check: \n","http://pydev.blogspot.com/2007/06/why-cant-pydev-debugger-work-with.html\n","to see how to restore the debug tracing back correctly.\n","Call Location:\n","  File \"/usr/lib/python3.11/bdb.py\", line 361, in set_quit\n","    sys.settrace(None)\n","\n"]}],"source":["%debug"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"VqSvySCeFPHD"},"source":["When you run `%debug`, you'll enter the debugger prompt `ipdb>`. Here are some common commands:\n","* `n` (next): Execute the next line of code.\n","* `s` (step): Step into a function call.\n","* `c` (continue): Continue execution until the next breakpoint or end of program.\n","* `q` (quit): Exit the debugger.\n","* `p variable_name`: Print the value of a variable.\n","* `l` (list): Show the current code context.\n","\n","#### Setting Breakpoints using `pdb` (Programmatic)\n","\n","You can explicitly set a breakpoint in your code using `breakpoint()` (Python 3.7+) or `import pdb; pdb.set_trace()` (older versions or explicit control)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"k2LAGa6QFPHD","outputId":"4abbd224-9fe4-4f40-bdd4-add952c712d3","executionInfo":{"status":"error","timestamp":1753417283070,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":5910,"user":{"displayName":"James Vasanth","userId":"02578488766480362375"}}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Summing numbers:\n","> \u001b[0;32m/tmp/ipython-input-19-4064926518.py\u001b[0m(7)\u001b[0;36msum_numbers\u001b[0;34m()\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0;32m      5 \u001b[0;31m        \u001b[0;31m# breakpoint() # For Python 3.7+\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m      6 \u001b[0;31m        \u001b[0;32mimport\u001b[0m \u001b[0mpdb\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m;\u001b[0m \u001b[0mpdb\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mset_trace\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m \u001b[0;31m# For older Python or explicit pdb\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m----> 7 \u001b[0;31m        \u001b[0mtotal\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m+=\u001b[0m \u001b[0mnum\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m      8 \u001b[0;31m        \u001b[0mprint\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34mf\"Current num: {num}, Current total: {total}\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m \u001b[0;31m# Just for display\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m      9 \u001b[0;31m    \u001b[0;32mreturn\u001b[0m \u001b[0mtotal\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0m\n","ipdb> q\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["\n","PYDEV DEBUGGER WARNING:\n","sys.settrace() should not be used when the debugger is being used.\n","This may cause the debugger to stop working correctly.\n","If this is needed, please check: \n","http://pydev.blogspot.com/2007/06/why-cant-pydev-debugger-work-with.html\n","to see how to restore the debug tracing back correctly.\n","Call Location:\n","  File \"/usr/lib/python3.11/bdb.py\", line 361, in set_quit\n","    sys.settrace(None)\n","\n"]}],"source":["def sum_numbers(data_list):\n","    total = 0\n","    for i, num in enumerate(data_list):\n","        # Set a breakpoint here to inspect 'num' and 'total' in each iteration\n","        # breakpoint() # For Python 3.7+\n","        import pdb; pdb.set_trace() # For older Python or explicit pdb\n","        total += num\n","        print(f\"Current num: {num}, Current total: {total}\") # Just for display\n","    return total\n","\n","print(\"Summing numbers:\")\n","result = sum_numbers([1, 2, 3, 4])\n","print(f\"Final result: {result}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["for i, num in enumerate([1,2,3,4]):\n","  print(\"Index \", i, \"has\",  num)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"2pIpZl79DHpq","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1749092768010,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":11,"user":{"displayName":"James Vasanth","userId":"02578488766480362375"}},"outputId":"88d9e8a4-6909-4148-cb10-ddde55462286"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Index  0 has 1\n","Index  1 has 2\n","Index  2 has 3\n","Index  3 has 4\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"bfV5_s49FPHD"},"source":["*(When you run the cell above, execution will pause at `pdb.set_trace()` and give you the `ipdb>` prompt.)*\n","\n","---\n","\n","### 3. Using IDEs for Debugging (More Powerful)\n","\n","While Jupyter is great for exploration, for serious coding and debugging, a dedicated IDE (Integrated Development Environment) is much more powerful. Popular IDEs for Python include:\n","\n","* **VS Code (Visual Studio Code):** Free, lightweight, highly customizable with extensions. Very popular.\n","* **PyCharm:** A full-featured, professional Python IDE (Community Edition is free). Excellent debugger.\n","* **Spyder:** Often comes with Anaconda, good for scientific computing with an R-like feel.\n","\n","#### Key Debugging Features in IDEs:\n","\n","1.  **Breakpoints:** Click in the gutter next to a line number to set/remove a breakpoint.\n","    * **Conditional Breakpoints:** Pause only if a certain condition is met (e.g., `i == 5`).\n","2.  **Step Over (F10 in VS Code/PyCharm):** Execute the current line and move to the next line. If the current line is a function call, it executes the *entire* function without stepping into it.\n","3.  **Step Into (F11):** Execute the current line. If it's a function call, it steps *into* that function's code.\n","4.  **Step Out (Shift+F11):** If you're inside a function, execute the rest of that function and stop at the line immediately after the function call.\n","5.  **Run to Cursor:** Execute code until the cursor's current position.\n","6.  **Variables/Watch Window:** A pane that shows the current values of all variables in the active scope. You can also \"watch\" specific expressions.\n","7.  **Call Stack:** Shows the sequence of function calls that led to the current point of execution.\n","8.  **Console/Terminal:** Interact with your program during debugging.\n","\n","#### How to Debug in a Typical IDE (Conceptual Steps):\n","\n","1.  **Open your Python file (`.py`).**\n","2.  **Set a breakpoint** at the line where you suspect an issue, or where you want to start investigating.\n","3.  **Start the debugger.** (Usually a \"Debug\" button or \"Run -> Start Debugging\").\n","4.  **Program execution pauses** at your first breakpoint.\n","5.  **Inspect variables** in the Variables window.\n","6.  **Use Step Over/Step Into** to move through your code line by line, observing how variable values change.\n","7.  **Identify the line** where the unexpected behavior or error occurs.\n","8.  **Understand the cause** by examining variable states at that point.\n","9.  **Fix the bug.**\n","10. **Restart the debugger** to verify the fix.\n","\n","**Example (Illustrative - no actual code to run here, but imagine doing this in an IDE):**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"0yR0seUeFPHD"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Imagine this code in VS Code or PyCharm\n","def process_data(data_list):\n","    transformed_data = []\n","    for item in data_list:\n","        # Set a breakpoint on the next line\n","        # Check 'item' value, check 'transformed_data' progress\n","        if item > 0:\n","            transformed_data.append(item * 2)\n","        else:\n","            # Maybe an unexpected negative value here?\n","            # Set another breakpoint here to check 'item' when it's <= 0\n","            transformed_data.append(0) # Let's say this is the bug, should be item * 3\n","    return transformed_data\n","\n","my_data = [1, 5, -2, 8, 0, 3]\n","result = process_data(my_data)\n","print(result) # Expected: [2, 10, 0, 16, 0, 6] but if bug exists, [-2, 0] would be handled differently"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"vnRlzz5TFPHD"},"source":["By stepping through this in an IDE, you'd quickly see `item` is `-2` and `item * 2` is applied, and then `0` is appended, leading to the bug.\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Conclusion\n","\n","Mastering Python is not just about writing code, but also about writing *good* code and being able to troubleshoot it effectively.\n","\n","* **`namedtuple` and `defaultdict`** from the `collections` module provide more robust and readable ways to handle common data patterns than basic tuples and dictionaries. They are particularly useful for structured data, counting, and grouping tasks.\n","* **Debugging** is an indispensable skill. While `print` statements are a quick fix, learning to use a debugger with **breakpoints** in an **IDE** like VS Code or PyCharm will dramatically increase your efficiency in finding and fixing issues in your code.\n","\n","Keep practicing these concepts, and you'll become a more proficient and confident Python developer!\n","\n","---"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"wB3X0tnFFPHD"},"source":["<div class=\"md-recitation\">\n","  Sources\n","  <ol>\n","  <li><a href=\"https://github.com/RemiJolian/Python-1402\">https://github.com/RemiJolian/Python-1402</a></li>\n","  </ol>\n","</div>"]}],"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[]},"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0}